- op: discuss  # 1c47
  at: '2026-07-21T23:32:51Z'  # 1c47
  by: agent  # 1c47
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1c47
  clock: 5  # 1c47
  nonce: 1c47  # 1c47
  message: "Closed by PR merged as dev 1c487b9973 (WI-zaziz). Root cause: smart-test selects tests via `hypergumbo slice --files` (an IMPORT-dependency reverse slice), blind to tests that COVER a source file through the analysis pipeline without IMPORTING it. Filed case: java.py changes selected test_java.py etc. but NOT test_polyglot_call_site_coverage.py (the sole cover of java.py:1872-1878, the static-import ExternalRef branch), false-redding the changed-file 100% coverage gate at 99% while the full suite is 100%; the manual manifest-add didn't survive auto-pr's commit-diff manifest regen.\n\nFIX (option b from the item): a checked-in declarative map .ci/coverage-only-deps.txt of source->covering-test pairs + scripts/coverage_only_deps.py helper, folded into AFFECTED_TESTS INSIDE smart-test (after the per-package fallback, before the manifest write) so the covering tests land in BOTH the run and the auto-pr-regenerated manifest — persisting across the commit-diff regeneration the manual workaround couldn't. Entries validated (source+test must exist on disk); a stale entry can neither disable the augmentation nor inject a phantom test.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: (1) 20 tests in tests/test_coverage_only_deps.py, helper at 100% coverage (parse_map / compute_adds / main / _read_lines all exercised in-process). (2) Direct real-map simulation: `echo java.py | coverage_only_deps.py . --map .ci/coverage-only-deps.txt --tests-file <test_java.py>` -> emits test_polyglot_call_site_coverage.py; a non-mapped source -> empty. (3) The committed-map guard test asserts every source+test in the live map exists on disk. (4) smart-test's own behavior tests (test_smart_test_slice_robustness, test_smart_test_coverage_gate) still pass with the added block. The augmentation fires whenever the mapped source is in CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES — confirmed present for a java.py change.\n\nFINDING (orthogonal, worth noting): the full end-to-end probe (touch java.py -> smart-test --manifest) fell to a FULL-SUITE fallback, not the targeted path, because the STABLE pipx hypergumbo 6.1.0 that smart-test uses for its internal slice still carries the WI-somup cold-cache bug ('Error: Input file not found: None' after a 402s cold analysis -> slice exit 1). WI-somup is `satisfied` on dev but evidently not yet in the released 6.1.0, so smart-test's internal slice fails on a genuinely-cold cache and falls back to full-suite. That is a separate release-lag/robustness matter (a successful-but-under-selecting slice is WI-zaziz's scope, which this fixes); flagging it here for follow-up.\n\nUnblocks WI-hokag (the deferred java shadowing-rename work) per the isbefore edge — the changed-file gate is now honest for java.py changes."  # 1c47
